## Query Source Layer Priority

When authoring SQL for query-based DAGs, prefer the immediate upstream analytical layer:

| Target layer | Preferred source layers | Avoid by default | Exception |
|---|---|---|---|
| **enrich** | `clean` and `enrich` | any direct `raw` read | No exception — `raw` is only for clean layer |
| **dw** | **`enrich` first** | direct `raw` / `clean` reads | Other `dw` only for explicit datamart DAGs |
| **metric** | **`dw` first** | datamart `dw` tables as primary source | Use non-datamart DW models as default inputs |

This guidance complements the cross-layer rule ("layer N may read layer N or below") with stronger defaults to reduce coupling and preserve modeling boundaries. In practice, `raw` should be consumed only by clean-layer DAGs.

