## Common Workflow Parameters

### All Query-Based Workflows (Enrich/DW/Metric)

```yaml
workflow:
    layer: "enrich"
    type: "query_delta"
    custom_schema: "banking"  # Optional
    default_extraction_type: "full"  # Optional: "full" or "incremental"
    default_partitions: []  # Optional
    default_table_privileges:  # Optional
        "prod-read-only": ["SELECT"]
        "prod-read-write": ["SELECT", "MODIFY", "APPLY TAG"]
    extra_query_template_params:  # Optional
        load_start_date: "{{ get_date_param(dag_run, macros.ds_add(data_interval_start | ds, -1), 'load_start_date') }}"
        load_end_date: "{{ get_date_param(dag_run, data_interval_start | ds, 'load_end_date') }}"
    inner_dependencies:  # Optional
        dependent_table:
            - dependency_table_1
            - dependency_table_2
    execution_timeout_hours: 2.0  # Optional
    has_hive_sync: true  # Optional
```

### Delta-Specific Parameters (query_delta workflows)

```yaml
workflow:
    run_vacuum: true  # Optional, default: true
    vacuum_retention_hours: 48  # Optional, default: 48
    vacuum_lite: true  # Optional, default: true; runtimes without LITE (DBR < 16.1) fall back to full VACUUM automatically
    run_optimize: true  # Optional, default: true on Databricks; on EMR, defaults to
                         # false unless the table has zorder columns (see below)
    tables_customization:
        table_name:
            merge_on: ["id", "date"]  # Optional, for upsert operations
            when_matched_update_condition: "source.ts_updated > target.ts_updated"  # Optional
            when_matched_delete_condition: "source.is_deleted = true"  # Optional
            when_not_matched_insert_condition: "source.is_valid = true"  # Optional
            z_order_by: ["user_id", "date"]  # Optional
            run_optimize: true  # Optional, explicit override always wins over engine defaults
            optimize_frequency_days: 7  # Optional, minimum days between OPTIMIZE runs
            table_properties:  # Optional
                delta.enableChangeDataFeed: "true"
            column_mapping_mode: name  # Optional — see #### column_mapping_mode below
            execution_timeout_hours: 3.0  # Optional
```

#### `column_mapping_mode` (`load_delta_table` only)

Per-table key: `tables_customization.<table>.column_mapping_mode`. Valid values: `none`, `name`, `id` (omit the key when the default is enough).

**Not recommended by default.** Column names with spaces, accents, or special characters do not follow [`naming_conventions.mdc`](naming_conventions.mdc). Prefer valid `snake_case` identifiers in SQL and omit this setting. Use `column_mapping_mode: name` only in **exceptional** cases — typically **reverse-layer** exports that must preserve a fixed downstream contract (legacy sheet headers, Oracle flexfield names) and cannot rename columns without breaking consumers.

| | |
|---|---|
| **Applies to** | `load_delta_table` Spark job only (`DeltaLoader` / `delta.columnMapping.mode`). |
| **Purpose** | Let Delta Lake store column names that are not valid identifiers. Without `name`, writes fail with `DELTA_INVALID_CHARACTERS_IN_COLUMN_NAMES`. |
| **Does not** | Map or rename columns in Google Sheets or other export targets. Downstream jobs read the Delta table schema as-is. |

```yaml
tables_customization:
    my_reverse_export:
        column_mapping_mode: name  # last resort: legacy headers cannot be renamed yet
```

#### `run_optimize` default on EMR

`OPTIMIZE ... ZORDER BY (...)` is a full shuffle/compaction and is proportionally far
more expensive on EMR (plain Delta OSS) than on Databricks. Unless `run_optimize` is
explicitly set (table-level `tables_customization.<table>.run_optimize`, or
workflow-level `run_optimize`), the default differs by engine:

- **Databricks** — unchanged: `run_optimize: true`, capped once per day via the
  existing `maintenance_once_per_day` marker.
- **EMR, table has no `z_order_by`/`raw_z_order_by`/`clean_z_order_by`** —
  `run_optimize` defaults to `false` (OPTIMIZE skipped). Set `run_optimize: true`
  explicitly if a specific table genuinely needs regular compaction despite no
  zorder columns.
- **EMR, table has zorder columns configured, OPTIMIZE runs full-table** —
  `run_optimize` defaults to `true`, and `optimize_frequency_days` defaults to
  `7` (weekly) instead of running every time the daily marker allows it.
  Override `optimize_frequency_days` per table (or at `workflow` level) if a
  table's read pattern needs tighter clustering.
- **EMR, table has zorder columns configured, but OPTIMIZE is partition-filtered**
  (TRANSACTIONAL-layer tables by default — opt out with `optimize_partition_filter: false`
  — or any table with `incremental_optimize: true` set table- or workflow-level) —
  `run_optimize` still defaults to `true`, but
  `optimize_frequency_days` stays `1` (daily) regardless of zorder. This is
  intentional: OPTIMIZE's `WHERE` clause only ever covers the current run's
  `load_start_date`..`load_end_date`, never the days elapsed since the last
  actual OPTIMIZE, so a weekly cadence on a partition-filtered table would
  leave 6 of every 7 days' partitions permanently un-optimized. Partition-filtered
  OPTIMIZE is already cheap (bounded to the run's date range), so daily is safe.

`VACUUM` is unaffected by any of the above — it keeps its own cadence/retention
(`run_vacuum`, `vacuum_retention_hours`, `maintenance_once_per_day`) regardless of
engine or `optimize_frequency_days`.

### Raw Database Pull Delta

```yaml
workflow:
    layer: "raw"
    type: "database_pull_delta"
    database_type: "postgres"  # Required: "postgres" or "mongo"
    dbutils_secret_key: "EBDB_DB"  # Optional, default: {CUSTOM_SCHEMA}_DB
    custom_schema: "ebdb"  # Optional
    default_extraction_type: "incremental"  # Optional
    lineage_product_database_name: "ebdb"  # Optional
    has_hive_sync: true  # Optional
    extra_query_template_params:  # Optional (Postgres only)
        load_start_date: "{{ get_date_param(dag_run, data_interval_start | ds, 'load_start_date') }}"
        load_end_date: "{{ get_date_param(dag_run, data_interval_start | ds, 'load_end_date') }}"
    tables_customization:  # Required
        raw_table_name:
            clean_table_name: "clean_table_name"  # Optional
            date_filter_column: "created_at"  # Optional, for incremental
            extraction_type: "incremental"  # Optional
            partitions: ["year", "month", "day"]  # Optional
            merge_on: ["id"]  # Optional
            z_order_by: ["user_id"]  # Optional
```

### Raw CDC

#### `source_schema` vs `source_database` — set correctly per database type

| Database type | `source_schema` | `source_database` |
|---------------|----------------|-------------------|
| **Postgres** | PostgreSQL schema name (usually `"public"`) | Database name (e.g. `"ebdb"`) |
| **MySQL** | Database name (same as `source_database`) | Database name (e.g. `"retsuko"`) |

Example — Postgres dag named `ebdb_condo`, tables in schema `public`:
```yaml
source_schema: "public"      # the PostgreSQL schema
source_database: "ebdb"      # the database name
custom_schema: "ebdb"        # destination schema in datalake (default: dag_name)
```

Example — MySQL dag named `retsuko`:
```yaml
source_schema: "retsuko"     # same as database name for MySQL
source_database: "retsuko"
```

#### Full CDC declaration

```yaml
workflow:
    layer: "raw"
    type: "cdc"
    database_type: "postgres"  # Required: "postgres" or "mysql"
    custom_schema: "ebdb"      # Optional, default: dag_name. Use for migration DAGs (e.g. "ebdb_test")
    source_database: "ebdb"    # Optional, default: custom_schema. Postgres DB name.
    source_schema: "public"    # Optional, default: "public". Postgres schema or MySQL DB name.
    dbutils_secret_key: "EBDB_DB"  # Optional. Default: <DESTINATION_SCHEMA>_DB (uppercase)
    lineage_product_database_name: "ebdb"  # Optional. Populate for full column-level lineage.
                                            # Leave empty for tag-level lineage only.
    has_hive_sync: true        # Optional. Check if tables will be queried from Trino.
    mysql_version: "8.0.30"    # Optional. MySQL connector version. Default: "8.0.30". MySQL only.
    tables_customization:      # Required
        table_name:            # CASE-SENSITIVE — must match source DB exactly
            clean_table_name: "clean_table_name"   # Optional, default: raw table name
            raw_primary_keys: ["id"]               # Optional, auto-detected by Spark job
            clean_primary_keys: ["id"]             # Optional, auto-detected by Spark job
            z_order_by: ["user_id"]                # Optional
            transactional_datatype_overrides:      # Optional
                column_name: "STRING"
            database_column_alias:                 # Optional
                year: "year_column"
            execution_timeout_hours: 3.0           # Optional
            collect_metrics: false                 # Optional. Collects count/avg/max/min from
                                                   # source DB. CAUTION: heavily impacts source DB.
```

#### Critical CDC caveats

- **Table names are case-sensitive**: `raw_table_name` keys in `tables_customization` must match the source database casing exactly (e.g. `Usuario`, not `usuario`).
- **All source tables must have primary keys**: Tables without PKs cannot be replicated by Debezium.
- **`debezium_signal` table**: Belongs in the Kafka connector config only — do NOT add it to `tables_customization` in the DAG declaration.
- **Migration testing**: Use `_test` suffix on the dag_name (e.g. `ebdb_condo_test` with `custom_schema: "ebdb_test"`) to run the CDC DAG side-by-side with the existing ingestion before replacing it.
- **CDC infrastructure is a prerequisite**: The Kafka Connect (Debezium) and S3-Sink connectors must already be deployed via Backstage before this DAG is created. Data must be visible in S3 `5a-datalake-incoming-{forno/prod}`.
- **Forno test is mandatory**: After creating the declaration + queries + metadata files, the DAG must run successfully on Forno Airflow before merging the PR.
- **`collect_metrics: true`**: Only enable if explicitly requested — it runs JDBC queries directly against the source database.
- **Adding tables to an existing CDC DAG**: Update the Kafka connector via Backstage first (`kafka-connect-add-tables`), then update the DAG declaration.

### Raw Custom Ingestion

```yaml
workflow:
    layer: "raw"
    type: "custom_ingestion"
    load_spark_job: "load_{extraction_type}_{dag_name}_into_datalake"  # Required
    spark_job_arguments:  # Required
        - "{environment}"
        - "{bucket}"
        - "{{ data_interval_start | ds }}"
        - "{table_name}"
    custom_schema: "api_source"  # Optional
    default_extraction_type: "incremental"  # Optional
    has_hive_sync: true  # Optional
    tables_customization:  # Required
        table_name:
            clean_table_name: "clean_table_name"  # Optional
            extraction_type: "incremental"  # Optional
            partitions: ["year", "month", "day"]  # Optional
            merge_on: ["id"]  # Optional
            extra_spark_job_arguments: ["extra_arg"]  # Optional
            raw_inner_dependencies:  # Optional
                dependent_raw_table:
                    - dependency_raw_table
            clean_inner_dependencies:  # Optional
                dependent_clean_table:
                    - dependency_clean_table
```

### Raw Gsheets

```yaml
workflow:
    layer: "raw"
    type: "gsheets"
    custom_schema: "gsheets"  # Required (historical reasons)
    has_hive_sync: true  # Optional
    credentials_scope: "quintoandar"  # Optional: quintoandar, people, mlops
```

**Naming rule**: DAG name must follow `gsheets_{business_context}` (e.g., `gsheets_cross`, `gsheets_for_sale`, `gsheets_growth`).

Gsheets also requires `forno_conf.yml` and `prod_conf.yml` with a `sheets_info` block. Each key is the raw table name; the DAG builder serializes the full entry and passes it to `load_gsheets_into_datalake.py` (no per-field wiring in the builder).

```yaml
# forno_conf.yml / prod_conf.yml
sheets_info:
  my_table:                              # raw table name (datalake_<custom_schema>_raw.my_table)
    sheet_id: "1AbCdEfGhIjKlMnOpQrStUvWxYz0123456789"  # Required
    sheet_name: "Sheet1"                 # Required — tab name inside the spreadsheet
    clean_table_name: my_table           # Required — clean query filename / datalake_<custom_schema>_clean target
    sheet_context: my_domain             # Required — business context (alerts, static-sheet routing)
    header_row: 5                        # Optional, default: 1 — 1-based row index used as column headers
    partitioned: true                    # Optional, default: false — add year/month/day partitions on load
    preload_time_in_seconds: 30          # Optional — sleep before fetching (rate-limited or slow sheets)
```

### Raw API Ingestion

Ingests data from REST APIs with configurable authentication and pagination. The `load_spark_job` defaults to `"load_api_ingestion_raw"` if not specified.

```yaml
workflow:
    layer: "raw"
    type: "api_ingestion"
    custom_schema: "my_api"          # Optional
    has_hive_sync: true              # Optional
    api_base_url: "https://api.example.com"   # Required — string (all envs) or dict per-env:
    # api_base_url:
    #   prod: "https://api.example.com"
    #   forno: "https://staging.example.com"
    authentication:                  # Required at workflow level OR per-table
        strategy: "oauth2_client_credentials"  # from AuthenticationStrategyEnum
        token_url: "https://auth.example.com/token"
        secret_key: "MY_API_SECRET"
        scopes: ["read"]             # Optional
    api_policies:                    # Optional
        rate_limiting:
            strategy: "fixed_delay"  # from RateLimitingStrategyEnum
            delay_seconds: 0.5
        pagination:
            strategy: "offset"       # from PaginationStrategyEnum
            page_size: 100
            limit_param: "limit"
            offset_param: "offset"
        error_handling:
            non_fatal_status_codes: [404]
            retry_policy:
                retries: 3
                delay: 5
                backoff_factor: 2
    extra_query_template_params:     # Optional — DAG-wide load_start_date / load_end_date
        load_start_date: "{{ get_date_param(dag_run, data_interval_start | ds, 'load_start_date') }}"
        load_end_date: "{{ get_date_param(dag_run, data_interval_start | ds, 'load_end_date') }}"
    tables_customization:            # Required
        my_endpoint:
            endpoint_path: "/v1/resources"   # Required per table
            # extra_query_template_params: # Optional: per-table date window (replaces workflow extra)
            #   load_end_date: "{{ get_date_param(dag_run, macros.ds_add(data_interval_start | ds, 1), 'load_end_date') }}"
            # authentication:              # Optional: override per-table authentication
            #     strategy: "api_key"
            #     api_key_field: "MY_KEY"
            #     location: "header"
            #     header_name: "X-API-Key"
```

