        ├── {dag_name}_declaration.yml  # Required
        ├── queries/
        │   ├── raw/  # For raw layer (if applicable)
        │   ├── clean/  # For clean layer
        │   ├── enrich/  # For enrich layer
        │   ├── dw/  # For DW layer
        │   └── metric/  # For metric layer
        ├── metadata/
        │   ├── clean/
        │   ├── enrich/
        │   ├── dw/
        │   └── metric/
        ├── data_quality/  # Optional
        │   ├── clean/
        │   ├── enrich/
        │   ├── dw/
        │   └── metric/
        └── spark_jobs/  # For custom Spark jobs
```

## Data Quality File Schema

Data quality files live at `data_quality/{layer}/{table_name}.yml`. They are optional but strongly encouraged for critical tables.

```yaml
table_name: schema_name.table_name   # fully qualified: schema.table
alert_channel: "#alerts-de-airflow-dags"   # Slack channel for DQ alerts
table_level_validations:
  has_size:
    greater_than: 0              # row count must exceed N
    severity_level: Error        # Error = blocks pipeline; Warning = logs only
column_level_validations:
  primary_key_col:
    is_complete:
      severity_level: Error      # no nulls allowed
    is_unique:
      severity_level: Error      # no duplicates
  important_col:
    is_complete:
      severity_level: Error
  nullable_col:
    has_completeness:
      greater_than: 0.95         # fraction non-null (0.0–1.0); allows up to 5% nulls
      severity_level: Warning
```

`severity_level: Error` fails the Airflow task and blocks downstream tasks. `Warning` logs the issue and allows the run to continue.

